																		Parawatch + Pride = Pridewatch
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349827" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1591308826 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jun 2020 22:13</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4676649">
									

<p>I had this idea at the start of the month and decided I wanted to have it out before the end of the week. It's based on several real-life things, such as MKULTRA and the CIA's dozens of attempts to kill Fidel Castro and failing miserably, but the story itself is (thankfully) fictional.</p>
<p>Thanks to DrFullham, MalyceGraves, Tuomey, DoctorDune, Cybersqyd, Coyolxauhqui and Tropiano for looking this over.</p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">I know the logo looks really pixelly, I'm seeing about getting it fixed.</span></p>
<p>E: Thanks to MalyceGraves for fixing up the logo! It can be found here for anyone who wants to add a bit of Pride to their Parawatch articles: <a href="http://firedawnfolder.wdfiles.com/local--files/somethingtested/parawatchPRIDE.png">http://firedawnfolder.wdfiles.com/local--files/somethingtested/parawatchPRIDE.png</a></p>

